  ('2a0efbd9-c6eb-4b4a-95f0-397ac9fc41fa','Milwaukee Kyudo Kai, based in Glendale, Wisconsin, is a USA Archery affiliated group running an Adult Archery Program, though its name points to something more specific than typical Western target archery: kyudo, the traditional Japanese art of the bow, which emphasizes form, ritual, and mental discipline as much as accuracy. That makes it a distinctive option in the Milwaukee area for adults drawn to a more meditative, traditionally rooted style of archery. As a hybrid group, it likely blends structured practice with a smaller, dedicated community of practitioners. Adults in the Glendale or greater Milwaukee area interested in kyudo should contact Milwaukee Kyudo Kai directly for current practice schedules.'),
  ('bdbe15f4-0562-41c5-bfed-9ddf88ff8d7f','MINARA Archery serves Albuquerque, New Mexico as a USA Archery affiliated club running both Junior Olympic Archery Development for young shooters and an Adult Archery Program for beginners of any age. That pairing gives the club a genuine on-ramp for families as well as adults new to the sport, in a metro area where dedicated archery facilities aren''t especially dense. As a hybrid club, it likely combines structured JOAD and adult coaching with a broader recreational membership base. Details on lane count or additional formats like 3D or field aren''t listed here. Anyone in the Albuquerque area interested in enrolling in JOAD or the adult program should contact MINARA Archery directly for current schedules.'),
  ('9f4ecaee-5d0f-4146-ba7f-0ad747913890','Minnehaha Archers, Inc. operates a 30-lane facility in Sioux Falls, South Dakota, a solid capacity that supports its USA Archery affiliated programming: Junior Olympic Archery Development, an Adult Archery Program, and field archery. Covering youth competitive training, adult beginners, and the outdoor field format all in one place makes it one of the more complete archery organizations in the region, well positioned to serve South Dakota''s largest metro area. The 30 lanes suggest room for leagues or group sessions without heavy scheduling conflicts. Families and adults in the Sioux Falls area interested in JOAD, adult programs, or field archery should contact Minnehaha Archers directly for current lane availability and schedules.'),
  ('32e03dfc-ee98-44e9-853a-a6acacdf9988','Minnesota Kyudo Renmei, based in Dundas, Minnesota, is a USA Archery affiliated group focused on kyudo, the traditional Japanese form of archery centered on posture, breath, and ritual as much as hitting the target, offered through its Adult Archery Program. That makes it a notably different option from the compound and Olympic-recurve clubs common across the state, appealing to adults drawn to a more contemplative, form-focused practice. Dundas sits just outside Northfield in southern Minnesota, putting the group within reach of the Twin Cities metro for those willing to travel. Adults interested in kyudo practice should contact Minnesota Kyudo Renmei directly for current session schedules and how to get started.'),
  ('f553c458-c92d-45dc-b1ca-f720bc9faddb','Mississippi Archery Academy, located in Pearl, Mississippi, is a USA Archery affiliated facility offering an unusually complete lineup: Junior Olympic Archery Development, an Adult Archery Program, 3D archery, field archery, and lessons. That range of formats and instruction covers nearly every entry point into the sport, from a child''s first JOAD session to an adult learning to shoot to hunters practicing 3D and field rounds. Pearl sits just outside Jackson, putting the academy within reach of central Mississippi''s largest metro area. Given the academy name and lesson offering, it appears built around teaching as much as providing range access. Archers interested in any of these programs should contact Mississippi Archery Academy directly for current schedules.'),
  ('9be27dcf-91c8-4801-909c-448e40b6eb5b','Mojave Archers, based in Helendale, California, is a USA Archery affiliated club running a Junior Olympic Archery Development program alongside both a 3D course and a field archery course, pairing youth competitive training with two distinct outdoor shooting formats. That''s a fairly rare combination, giving members and young JOAD archers room to work on precision target shooting, judged 3D distances, and the varied terrain of a field course all in one place. Helendale sits in the high desert of the Mojave region, offering open, rugged terrain well suited to outdoor course archery. Interested archers or JOAD families should contact Mojave Archers directly for current schedules and course access.'),
  ('38855409-e8ed-4ce8-863c-35f2b74e2888','Monroe County Bowhunters is a volunteer-run 3D archery club in Atmore, Alabama, affiliated with the Archery Shooters Association, putting it firmly in the bowhunting-practice tradition of judged-distance foam target shooting. That ASA tie suggests a membership focused on sharpening shot placement and range estimation ahead of Alabama''s hunting seasons rather than pure Olympic-style target work. Cole Byrd is listed as a contact for the club, a useful first call for anyone in the Atmore area wanting to shoot the course or explore membership. Being volunteer-run, the club likely depends on member dues and labor to maintain its grounds. Reach out to Cole Byrd or the club directly for current access and membership details.'),
  ('29fb651a-33ef-4603-b33a-3b0d8c7dad27','On the Cape Cod Canal side of Bourne, Massachusetts, Monument Beach Sportsmans Club runs its archery program under USA Archery affiliation, with both a Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) track and an Adult Archery Program on offer. That combination means the club is set up to take a shooter from a first draw all the way through structured, scored competition, rather than just hosting casual open shooting. Coastal Massachusetts doesn''t have an enormous archery scene, so a JOAD-affiliated club in this corner of the state is a notable resource for families looking for coached, progression-based instruction. Exact schedules and membership costs aren''t posted here, so reaching out to the club directly is the right next step.'),
  ('82955337-e728-4f16-9ec3-65f09552757c','Vass, North Carolina, tucked into the Sandhills near Fort Liberty, is where Moore Co Bowhunters of NC keeps its ASA-affiliated 3D archery course running. ASA affiliation points toward a scored, foam-animal target format that draws a bowhunting crowd looking to sharpen range estimation and shot placement before deer season, more than a group focused on Olympic-style target rounds. Amber Chavis is listed as the club''s contact, a good first call for anyone wanting to know shoot dates, course conditions, or how a newcomer gets involved. As with most volunteer-run clubs, day-to-day hours aren''t fixed or posted publicly, so confirming details ahead of a visit is worth the effort.'),
  ('17a2a423-08d9-4389-8fa6-b7209e791da3','East Tennessee''s Morristown Archery Club runs as an ASA-affiliated 3D archery operation, putting it in the same competitive circuit as many of the region''s bowhunting-focused clubs. The ASA tie generally means foam-animal targets scored at varying, unmarked distances, a format built to sharpen the kind of judgment bowhunters need in the field rather than fixed-distance target rounds. Junior Sizemore serves as the listed contact, which is the practical starting point for anyone wanting to learn shoot dates or how to join. Like most volunteer clubs in this part of Tennessee, the group doesn''t appear to post regular public hours, so reaching out ahead of a visit is the way to get accurate, current information.'),
  ('abbdee3c-176a-41e3-a9b6-40e2797cf7b2','Cortland sits in Ohio''s Trumbull County, and Mosquito Bowmen is the ASA-affiliated 3D club serving archers in that corner of the state, not far from Mosquito Lake itself. An ASA affiliation signals a 3D, animal-target format aimed at bowhunters honing distance judgment and shot placement, a common thread among clubs in Ohio''s northeast. Brenda Zannetakis is the contact on record, a reasonable first stop for questions about course access, shoot schedules, or membership. Beyond the affiliation, the listing doesn''t include lane counts, amenities, or a fixed course description, which tracks with how most volunteer-run 3D clubs operate on member time rather than posted public hours, so a direct inquiry is the best way to get specifics.'),
  ('2654591f-7221-4d04-acab-b8b2b279d4b7','Mountain State Sportsmen Association operates out of Parkersburg, West Virginia, near the Ohio River, and its listing carries an ASA affiliation, though the record on file shows that status expired for 2025. That doesn''t necessarily mean the club has stopped running archery activities, just that its formal ASA membership isn''t confirmed current, so anyone counting on sanctioned 3D shoots there should check directly. Clubs built around a broader sportsmen''s association, rather than archery alone, often fold archery in alongside hunting and fishing programming. Specific hours and current membership status aren''t listed here, making a direct call the only reliable way to get current information.'),
  ('8ac734e9-4fca-4642-8aed-9dfb8bdee893','Muddy Bayou Archery Inc., based in Gallatin just northeast of Nashville, is a USA Archery affiliated club that stacks together an unusually full slate of programming: Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) for younger shooters, an Adult Archery Program, 3D Archery, and Field Archery, plus lessons for people starting from scratch. That breadth means a beginner could take lessons, a junior could work through JOAD''s structured progression, and a bowhunter could still get 3D practice, all under one roof rather than needing separate clubs for each. Middle Tennessee has a solid archery community, and a hybrid club offering both Olympic-style and 3D formats is a genuine draw for archers who don''t want to be boxed into one discipline.'),
