  ('21b68e82-73d8-4868-8660-ddc694a215c4','Neshoba County Bowmen is based in Philadelphia, Mississippi, home to the annual Neshoba County Fair, and carries an ASA affiliation on record, though that status shows as expired for 2025. That doesn''t necessarily mean the club has stopped shooting archery, only that its formal ASA membership isn''t confirmed current, so anyone hoping to shoot a sanctioned round should verify status directly. East-central Mississippi has a steady bowhunting culture, and a county-named club like this typically functions as the area''s main organized archery outlet. Hours and current activity level aren''t listed here, so reaching out to the club directly is the only reliable way to get accurate information.'),
