  ('b21459b7-8dcf-4aff-b995-188c9cf47350','Nevada County JOAD runs its Junior Olympic Archery Development program under USA Archery affiliation out of Nevada City, in the Sierra Nevada foothills of Northern California. As a JOAD-focused operation without a separate adult program listed, the club''s identity centers on developing younger archers through a structured, scored progression rather than serving as an all-ages open range. Nevada City''s small-town setting in gold country doesn''t have a huge archery scene, so a dedicated JOAD program stands out as one of the more organized youth options in that part of the foothills. Program schedules, fees, and facility specifics aren''t detailed here, so parents interested in enrolling a young archer should contact the program directly for current information.'),
  ('72a6e39d-d125-4a80-b36e-9a92820c9638','New England School of Archery, operating as NESA LLC out of Concord, New Hampshire, is a USA Archery affiliated program running both Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) and an Adult Archery Program. The school framing in its name points to an operation built around instruction and progression more than a walk-in range. Being based in the state capital gives it reasonably central access for archers across central New Hampshire, and offering both a youth pathway and adult programming lets a family train together rather than splitting across separate clubs. Specific class schedules and pricing aren''t listed here, so contacting NESA directly is the way to learn what''s currently offered.'),
