  ('f3374a68-06ee-40aa-a7d0-5d3cb16d2bc1','Passin Time Archery is a club in Sparta, Tennessee, on the Cumberland Plateau in the middle of the state, listed with an ASA archery club affiliation whose status is recorded as expired in 2025. That expired status is worth flagging up front, since it suggests the club''s formal ASA tie may have lapsed even if the group is still active locally, which is common when smaller clubs don''t renew annually. No pro shop, lessons program, 3D course, or field course is confirmed here either way. Sparta''s Cumberland Plateau setting has a solid rural hunting culture that a club like this likely serves regardless of its current ASA standing. Anyone interested should contact Passin Time Archery directly to confirm whether it''s still active and what it currently offers.'),
  ('b59cdb05-d34e-4892-bd74-430a6a93f60b','Tucked into the wooded hill country near Birdseye, Indiana, Patoka Lake Bowhunters runs as a volunteer-organized club with an ASA affiliation, placing it squarely in the 3D archery and bowhunting circuit that''s popular across southern Indiana. That ASA connection usually points to a group built around realistic animal targets and scored field rounds rather than paper-target precision alone, which tends to draw archers who also hunt. Don Rohlman is listed as the club''s contact, a solid first call for anyone wanting to know about shoot schedules, course conditions, or how membership works, since day-to-day operations aren''t posted publicly. Southern Indiana''s mix of state forest and farmland makes this a natural gathering spot for local bowhunters.'),
  ('646138e1-1499-446a-bd18-235ad2da8733','Pawnee Bow Range in Pawnee, Oklahoma is a volunteer-run club carrying an ASA affiliation, which ties it into the same 3D and bowhunting-oriented circuit found across much of rural Oklahoma. Clubs with that ASA tie generally structure their year around scored 3D shoots using animal targets, appealing to archers who hunt as much as they compete. Jayme Buchanan is the listed contact, worth reaching out to for anything beyond the basics, since the club doesn''t appear to publish detailed hours or course information. Pawnee County''s open land and hunting culture make a member-run range like this a natural fit for the area, though specifics on the course layout and membership process are best confirmed directly with Buchanan.'),
  ('093aa65e-fe2b-44cf-ad01-5390f4c6af4e','In Carthage, Mississippi, Pearl River Archery runs as a volunteer club with an ASA affiliation, putting it in the same 3D archery and bowhunting network found throughout much of the state. That affiliation usually means a shooting calendar built around scored animal-target rounds rather than strictly indoor target work, drawing a hunting-minded membership. Jarvis Hamilton is listed as the person to contact, a useful starting point for questions about shoot dates or how to join, since the club doesn''t appear to have detailed public hours. Carthage sits in Mississippi''s central hill country, an area with a strong deer-hunting tradition that fits well with an ASA-style club''s focus on realistic 3D targets and hunting-season preparation.'),
  ('9c11c374-51d0-4af6-92c2-d02ef10bf004','Pekin Archers N.F.P., based in Pekin, Illinois, is a volunteer club with an ASA affiliation, connecting it to the broader 3D archery and bowhunting circuit active across central Illinois. The not-for-profit designation and volunteer structure suggest a group run by its own members rather than paid staff, typical of long-running small-town archery clubs in the region. Nancy Kerley is listed as the contact for the club, the right first stop for questions about shoot schedules, course access, or membership, since detailed public information isn''t posted here. Central Illinois has a solid bowhunting base, and an ASA-affiliated club like this one likely serves as a seasonal hub for archers gearing up for deer season.'),
  ('82c31aa4-b632-4334-9395-037415722680','Penn Del Archers in Garnet Valley, Pennsylvania is a USA Archery affiliated club that runs an Adult Archery Program alongside lessons, a 3D course, and a field course, making it a fairly full-service option for archers of different skill levels in the Philadelphia suburbs. Having both 3D and field layouts on-site is relatively uncommon and lets members practice varied shooting styles without traveling between locations. The lesson offering means newcomers have a real entry point rather than needing to already own gear and know the fundamentals. Garnet Valley sits in Delaware County, within reach of a large suburban population, so a club with this range of programming is likely to draw archers from across the southeastern Pennsylvania area.'),
  ('976d0586-1cf4-47cd-bcf5-615ddc1ef696','Percy Quin Archery, based in McComb, Mississippi, is a volunteer club carrying an ASA affiliation, linking it to the state''s 3D archery and bowhunting circuit. The name likely nods to nearby Percy Quin State Park, a common reference point for clubs in this part of southwest Mississippi. An ASA tie typically means a schedule built around scored animal-target rounds, appealing to members who hunt as well as compete. James Whittington is the listed contact, the best way to get specifics on shoot dates, course conditions, or membership, since public details beyond the affiliation aren''t posted. McComb sits in a heavily wooded region of the state with strong deer-hunting traditions, a natural fit for an ASA-style club''s focus.'),
  ('86799600-b66b-48b7-82e8-4392ae0a5125','The Permian Basin Archers Association in Odessa, Texas is a USA Archery affiliated club running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development (JOAD) program and an Adult Archery Program, covering youth and grown-up archers under one roof. Having a JOAD pathway in an oil-country city like Odessa gives young archers in the Permian Basin a structured, competition-oriented path that isn''t always available in smaller West Texas towns. The parallel adult program suggests the club isn''t purely youth-focused, and instead builds a shooting community across age groups. West Texas archery options can be sparse given the distances between towns, so a dual-program USA Archery club based in Odessa likely draws members from a fairly wide surrounding area.'),
  ('46ad9a01-dc1b-46e2-8dec-bcf7db152b51','Philly Archery is a USA Archery affiliated club in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania offering both an Adult Archery Program and lessons, positioning it as an approachable entry point for grown-ups picking up a bow for the first time in the city. The pairing of a structured adult program with actual instruction suggests this club leans toward building new archers rather than only serving people who already shoot competitively. Being USA Archery affiliated also connects members to the national governing body''s coaching standards and event pathways. In a dense city like Philadelphia, a club focused specifically on adult participation fills a gap for archers who missed youth programs like JOAD growing up and are picking up the sport later in life.'),
  ('d29dcd96-afe3-49de-8e5c-902c5634b13c','Phoenix Focus JOAD, based in Anthem, Arizona just north of Phoenix, is a USA Archery affiliated club running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program. The JOAD name front and center signals a club built primarily around developing young archers through USA Archery''s structured youth pathway, while the parallel adult program means parents or other grown-ups in the area have a way to shoot alongside their kids'' program rather than being left out. Anthem''s fast-growing north Phoenix location puts the club within reach of a large and expanding suburban population. Families in the area looking for a competition-oriented youth archery program, with adult participation built in, would find this club worth contacting directly for enrollment details.'),
  ('ca65d651-124f-4adf-9131-0a59b0deeb41','Piedra Bowhunters, Inc. operates out of Monte Vista, Colorado as a volunteer club with an ASA affiliation, placing it in the San Luis Valley''s small but active bowhunting community. The ASA tie generally means the club''s calendar centers on scored 3D shoots with animal targets, which lines up well with the region''s strong big-game hunting tradition. Stephanie Gallegos is listed as the club''s contact, a good starting point for questions about shoot dates, course access, or membership, since detailed public hours aren''t posted. Monte Vista sits in a high-altitude valley ringed by mountains with heavy elk and deer hunting pressure each fall, making an ASA-affiliated bowhunting club a natural fit for archers preparing for the season.'),
  ('7a2a6c93-a122-4aea-ad8d-ad7fc1e10589','Pinckney Pirate Archers, taking its name from the local high school mascot, is a USA Archery affiliated club in Pinckney, Michigan running a Junior Olympic Archery Development program. The JOAD focus points to a youth-oriented club built around USA Archery''s structured pathway toward competitive target archery, likely drawing on the school community given the Pirate name. Southeast Michigan has a decent cluster of JOAD programs, and a club tied to a specific town like Pinckney often serves as the local option for families who don''t want to drive to a bigger metro program in Ann Arbor or Detroit. Anyone interested in enrolling a young archer should reach out directly for schedule and registration details.'),
  ('bdb5e25c-bd59-45c9-8a86-71a435668587','Pine Ridge Archery, located in Indian Mound, Tennessee, is a volunteer club with an ASA affiliation, connecting it to the 3D archery and bowhunting circuit active across the state''s rural counties. Indian Mound sits in a heavily wooded part of Stewart County near the Kentucky border, an area with a strong deer-hunting tradition that fits naturally with ASA''s animal-target format. Joey Wright is listed as the club''s contact, the right person to reach for details on shoot schedules, course conditions, or how to join, since public hours aren''t posted here. For bowhunters in the northwest Tennessee area looking for a scored 3D shooting circuit, Pine Ridge Archery is a local option worth a direct call.'),
  ('44d0a9e7-94ed-487b-acd5-cb82428d185f','Pineapple Archery in Glendale, Arizona is a club that offers both a 3D course and lessons, giving it real facilities and structure beyond a bare membership listing. Its record shows an ASA affiliation, though that status is noted as expired for 2025, so its current standing with the organization isn''t something to assume without checking directly with the club. The combination of on-site 3D shooting and instruction suggests it has historically served both experienced 3D archers and newcomers looking to learn under one roof in the Phoenix metro area. Glendale''s suburban population gives a club like this a solid local base to draw from. Anyone interested should confirm current ASA status, hours, and program availability directly with Pineapple Archery before visiting.'),
  ('427d5307-27fa-4361-b223-cd2217e2e469','Pineapple JOAD is a USA Archery affiliated club in Glendale, Arizona running a Junior Olympic Archery Development program, giving young archers in the West Phoenix suburbs a structured, competition-track option. The JOAD-only focus here suggests the club''s programming centers specifically on youth development within USA Archery''s national pathway rather than a broader mix of adult or recreational offerings. Glendale is a large, growing part of the Phoenix metro, and a dedicated JOAD club provides local families an alternative to driving further into the city for youth archery instruction. No further detail on lanes, course type, or hours is listed here, so parents interested in enrolling a young archer should contact the program directly for specifics.')
